cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this experiment, please cite it as below."
title: "ClaudeExperiment: an AI-assisted formalization on dialogue-tree height in Gödel's System T"
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked Agda prototypes and a first-person report from an AI system
  (Claude, across Claude Fable 5 and Claude Opus 4.8) working on Martín Escardó's
  conjecture that the dialogue-tree height of a System T term of type
  (iota => iota) => iota is below epsilon_0. The Agda code and report were
  authored by Claude and supervised by Martín Escardó. The experiment lives in
  source/Claude/ and is an Agda library depending on TypeTopology (which supplies
  the imported modules; checked against commit bae60c78). The conjecture remains
  open. Nothing here is committed to TypeTopology itself, and there is no
  intention to do so.
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "Claude (Claude Fable 5 and Claude Opus 4.8)"
    alias: Claude
    website: "https://www.anthropic.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/martinescardo/ClaudeExperiment"
date-released: 2026-07-10
keywords:
  - Agda
  - System T
  - dialogue trees
  - ordinal analysis
  - epsilon-nought
  - AI-assisted mathematics
  - TypeTopology
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "The conjecture, and the supervision of this work"
    authors:
      - family-names: Escardó
        given-names: Martín
